@ryandasilva175 They are metric to begin with. Go to auto part store. Explain your situation, they will show you the plug you need, then you ask for the METRIC socket , 6 point, deep well 3/8 inch drive. 
A 8 inch long length of rubber fuel line will do nicely re-installing the plugs GENTLEY until somewhat seated, then go back to the socket to tighten to spec. The rubber tube also helsp in extracting the plugs from the deep holes. 

Have fun!

@CarlosGarcia-qm8fq The MAS/MAF sensor is a really common culprit for issues like that on [PLATE REDACTED].7L Dodge engines. Before replacing it, sometimes a good cleaning with MAF cleaner spray can fix the issue. If that doesn't work, replacement is usually straightforward.

We have a video on troubleshooting those types of misfires and sensor issues that might help you narrow it down: https://youtu.be/XuDnxoAos9g

Good luck, hope you get that 4.7L running smoothly!

