@diyeric5072 hey bud mind if I ask you which brand coil you replaced with? My [PLATE REDACTED] civic [PLATE REDACTED].8l had #2 cylinder misfire, and p0401 egr insufficient flow. Took it to local shop they used one of the local auto parts places to replace coil and egr. And cleared codes. Egr code came back after readiness monitors were set. The misfire came back about a month later. The aftermarket coil was junk. Still chasing the egr issue. Anyway I bought 4 used coils from ebay for $30 put the oem coil on and misfire gone. Plus I now have 3 more good coils. 

I cleaned oem egr removed tube going to exhaust below cat ran a pipe cleaner through it to make sure there were no blockages. Used my snap on verus pro to test egr through functional tests. It made me bring engine temp up to 186 degrees fahrenheit and hold rpm between 2500 [PLATE REDACTED] rpm for approx 5 minutes during test. Test came back everything was normal. I checked pin drag on connector and everything felt fine. I checked voltages for [PLATE REDACTED] wires and everything checked out there as well. Bench tested egr valve and it was fine. Not sure now what direction to go. Thinking possibly map sensor. I'm going to clean it and possibly replace it. 

Son bought the car used and head was replaced right before he got it, not sure if it was overheated and reason head was changed but possibly the heat if that did happen couldn't possibly damage map sensor. When looking at data map is within specs but with out scoping it no telling if there's a glitch or drop out scanner may not be seeing?
